=\frac{\sin(200\pi t)}{\pi t}.\] At \(t=0\), use the standard limit \[\lim_{t\to 0}\frac{\sin(at)}{t}=a.\] Hence, \[h(0)=\frac{200\pi}{\pi}=200.\] \[\boxed{200}\] <div class="sol-block sol-keypoints"><div class="sol-block-title">Key points</div><ul><li>For an ideal LPF with cutoff frequency \(\omega_c\), \(h(t)=\dfrac{\sin(\omega_c t)}{\pi t}\).</li><li>The value at the origin is \(h(0)=\dfrac{\omega_c}{\pi}\).</li></ul></div>

