\frac{14.142}{40}\times\frac{1}{2}\] \[R_{ext}=23.28\,\Omega\] \[\boxed{A}\] <div class="sol-block sol-keypoints"><div class="sol-block-title">Key points</div><ul><li>In a DC series motor, \(\phi_{se}\propto I_a\) before saturation.</li><li>Electromagnetic torque is proportional to \(I_a^2\).</li><li>Back emf relation is \(E_a\propto \phi N\).</li></ul></div> <div class="sol-block sol-mistakes"><div class="sol-block-title">Mistakes to avoid</div><ul><li>Do not use constant flux relation as in shunt motors.</li><li>Use \(T_L\propto N^3\) carefully while comparing torque.</li><li>Use the new speed ratio as \(N'/N=1/2\).</li></ul></div>

