4^\circ\] Also, \[X_s=2\,\Omega\] and stator resistance is negligible. <div class="sol-block sol-method"><div class="sol-block-title">Method 1</div>The armature current is \[I=\frac{V-E}{jX_s}\] Hence, \[|I|=\frac{|V-E|}{X_s}\] Since \(|V|=|E|\) and the angle between them is \(4^\circ\), \[|V-E|
=
\sqrt{V^2+E^2-2VE\cos(4^\circ)}\] \[=
\sqrt{2V^2\left(1-\cos(4^\circ)\right)}\] \[=
1905.26\sqrt{2\left(1-\cos(4^\circ)\right)}\] Using \[\cos(4^\circ)\approx 0.99756\] \[1-\cos(4^\circ)\approx 0.00244\] \[|V-E|
=
1905.26\sqrt{2(0.00244)}\] \[=
1905.26\sqrt{0.00488}\] \[\approx 1905.26(0.06984)
\approx 133.5\,\text{V}\] Therefore, \[|I|
=
\frac{133.5}{2}
\approx 66.75\,\text{A}\]</div> \[\boxed{66.75}\] <div class="sol-block sol-keypoints"><div class="sol-block-title">Key points</div><ul><li>For negligible armature resistance, \[I=\frac{V-E}{jX_s}.\]</li><li>The magnitude of current depends on the phasor difference between \(V\) and \(E\).</li><li>Mechanical angle and electrical angle are related by \[\delta_{elec}
