+\sin\!\left(5\omega t+\frac{\pi}{2}\right)\] The fundamental, third and fifth harmonic components are \[i_1(t)=10\sin\!\left(\omega t-\frac{\pi}{6}\right)\] \[i_3(t)=2\sin\!\left(3\omega t+\frac{\pi}{6}\right)\] \[i_5(t)=\sin\!\left(5\omega t+\frac{\pi}{2}\right)\] Hence, \[I_{1,\mathrm{RMS}}=\frac{10}{\sqrt{2}},\qquad
I_{3,\mathrm{RMS}}=\frac{2}{\sqrt{2}},\qquad
I_{5,\mathrm{RMS}}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\] The effective RMS current is \[I_{\mathrm{eff(RMS)}}
=
\sqrt{I_{1,\mathrm{RMS}}^{2}
+I_{3,\mathrm{RMS}}^{2}
+I_{5,\mathrm{RMS}}^{2}}\] \[=
\sqrt{\left(\frac{10}{\sqrt2}\right)^2
+\left(\frac{2}{\sqrt2}\right)^2
+\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt2}\right)^2}
=
7.246\,\text{A}\] The distortion factor is \[\mathrm{DF}
=
\frac{I_{1,\mathrm{RMS}}}{I_{\mathrm{eff(RMS)}}}
=
\frac{10/\sqrt2}{7.246}
=
0.976\] The displacement power factor is \[\cos\theta
